{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>For</b> — He says: \"For bulls have surrounded me\" and other enemies who are lesser than the bulls yet more provoking, and they are a band of evildoers. And the meaning of \"like a lion\" is joined with \"they surrounded me\": they surrounded me like a lion." "<b>My hands and my feet</b> — And he mentioned \"my hands,\" for with them one fights, and \"my feet,\" for with them one can flee."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "I read והם עדת מרעים as referring to the \"other enemies\"; the comparison \"lesser than the bulls yet more provoking\" echoes the psalm's own progression from bulls (v. 13) to dogs (v. 17)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:15.490784699Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}